59	2608.06192	HOPE: Hand-Object Pressure Estimation from Monocular Videos	Estimating physical pressure from vision is essential for understanding contact-rich hand-object interaction. However, prior vision-based pressure estimation methods are largely limited to planar surfaces and single image input, making them difficult to apply to dynamic hand-object interaction with diverse objects. We instead formulate pressure estimation as a hand-centric video prediction problem with monocular video as input. This formulation predicts temporally evolving per-vertex normal pressure and contact directly on the hand mesh, yielding a unified output space independent of object shape and sensor layout. Building on this formulation, we propose \\textbf{HOPE}, a framework with two key components. First, we lift tactile-glove pressure, planar-sensor pressure, and distance-based hand-object contact annotations into a shared hand vertex space, allowing bare-hand contact data to regularize pressure learning where metric labels are unavailable. Second, we introduce a vertex-anchored video transformer that treats each vertex as a persistent token, aggregates visual features and hand pose over time, and uses a contact-gated pressure head to enforce that pressure vanishes without contact. Experiments on OpenTouch, PressureVisionDB, and hand-object contact benchmarks validate HOPE across object-pressure, surface-pressure, and contact-supervised HOI settings. Despite using metric pressure supervision primarily from gloved-hand videos, HOPE generalizes to bare-hand egocentric and in-the-wild videos, producing joint contact and pressure predictions beyond the scope of contact-only or planar-pressure baselines.	2026-08-06 15:51:46+00	2026-08-06 15:51:46+00	https://arxiv.org/pdf/2608.06192v1	{cs.CV}	https://openalex.org/W7201869393	\N	0	2	1.764	EMBEDDED	{"arxiv_id_versioned": "2608.06192v1", "authors_raw": ["Subin Jeon", "Byungjun Kim", "Hanbyul Joo"], "primary_category": "cs.CV", "comment": "project page is at: https://subin6.github.io/page-hope", "doi": null, "openalex": {"openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/W7201869393", "cited_by_count": 0, "referenced_works_count": 0, "publication_year": 2026, "type": "preprint", "authorships": [{"name": "Subin Jeon", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5028007737", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Byungjun Kim", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5146029045", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Hanbyul Joo", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5145981559", "affiliation": null}], "concepts": [{"name": "Artificial intelligence", "score": 0.6251000165939331}, {"name": "Computer vision", "score": 0.6159999966621399}, {"name": "Computer science", "score": 0.5789999961853027}, {"name": "Lift (data mining)", "score": 0.5188000202178955}, {"name": "Monocular", "score": 0.5159000158309937}]}, "hn": {"mentions": 2, "total_points": 14, "top_story_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=24268698", "top_story_points": 13}}	2026-08-07 13:50:22.419217+00	2026-08-29 16:24:27.884173+00
225	2608.27421	Learning a Continuous Sepsis Severity Score Without Hour-by-Hour Supervision: A Two-Site Retrospective Study	Currently used sepsis severity indices rely on fixed variables and weights established decades ago, which are coarsely discretized and calibrated to a cohort that no longer reflects contemporary critical care. No alternative learned directly from patient trajectories is in routine use. We conducted a retrospective two-cohort study on a total of 29,116 and 7,691 adult patients meeting Sepsis-3 criteria from two hospital systems in Massachusetts and Georgie, respectively.\n  We developed a sepsis index using 43 routinely charted variables over a 72-hour treatment window. Unlike previous studies, we use mortality as a treatment-level ranking signal rather than a per-state target, allowing credit to be redistributed non-uniformly across timesteps. Evaluation was done on a permanent 20% test holdout, using clinical vignettes and Spearman correlation. Uncertainty intervals were obtained by bootstrap resampling of whole patients. Under this ranking scheme, non-survivors scored 1.19-1.64 points higher than survivors on a 0-10 scale within all strata of baseline SOFA-2, with similar results stratifying within lactate, mean arterial pressure (MAP), and creatinine. Within-patient change in the index correlated with change in lactate (Spearman rho = 0.39; n = 1,854). Similar, weaker correlations were found for MAP and creatinine. On a cohort level, cross-institutional agreement measured by Spearman correlation between models trained on different sites, were 70-77% of same-site correlation. External within-patient correlations were 0.54 and 0.59 against ceilings of 0.92 and 0.90. Our index also correlated with established indices, while null controls stayed near zero.\n  Our index demonstrated hourly prognostic information that meaningfully separates patient outcomes and is consistent with clinical expectation, indicating potential as a decision support tool complementing clinical judgement.	2026-08-27 17:46:21+00	2026-08-27 17:46:21+00	https://arxiv.org/pdf/2608.27421v1	{cs.AI,cs.LG}	https://openalex.org/W7204573355	\N	0	1	1.167	EMBEDDED	{"arxiv_id_versioned": "2608.27421v1", "authors_raw": ["Kevin Zhu", "Ryan Zhang", "Baraa Abed", "Tilendra Choudhary", "Malvern Madondo", "Mehak Arora", "Yixuan Yang", "Alasdair Gent", "Aditya Nagori", "Omer T. Inan", "Krista L. Haines", "Patrick Georgoff", "Suresh M. Agarwal", "Vijay Krishnamoorthy", "Tetsu Ohnuma", "Mihai V. Podgoreanu", "Michael R. Pinsky", "Gilles Clermont", "Craig M. Coopersmith", "Craig S. Jabaley", "Rishikesan Kamaleswaran"], "primary_category": "cs.AI", "comment": null, "doi": null, "openalex": {"openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/W7204573355", "cited_by_count": 0, "referenced_works_count": 0, "publication_year": 2026, "type": "preprint", "authorships": [{"name": "Kevin Zhu", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5148515354", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Ryan Zhang", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5148530368", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Baraa Abed", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5119381014", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Tilendra Choudhary", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5037399650", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Malvern Madondo", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5008694757", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Mehak Arora", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5148548899", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Yixuan Yang", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5148478278", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Alasdair Gent", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5134186218", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Aditya Nagori", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5005766528", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Omer T. Inan", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5121921621", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Krista Haines", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5037057113", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Patrick Georgoff", "openalex_id": "