77	2608.06146	PaDoc: Layout-Grounded Parallel Decoding for Document Parsing	End-to-end document parsers provide a unified interface, but serialize page layouts and regional contents into one autoregressive sequence. This formulation forces independent regions onto a decoding path whose length grows with the total content, whereas crop-based two-stage parsers expose region-level parallelism at the cost of repeated visual prefills and fragmented page context. To retain full-page context while removing dependencies, we propose PaDoc, a layout-grounded parser that treats the predicted layout as a branching structure over a shared page representation. Under a region-sufficiency assumption, we derive a prefix-conditioned factorization in which the layout stream and regional content branches advance concurrently, reducing the decoding depth to the longest layout-content path. We realize this factorization within a single MLLM: packed variable-length ancestor attention preserves the visibility under standard next-token training, while masked parallel decoding creates branches that the evaluated vLLM backend serves as concurrent requests with cache-resident shared-prefix reuse. On OmniDocBench Full, PaDoc attains an Overall layout F1 of 91.1 and, among end-to-end parsers, a top-tier Overall score of 94.24 together with the best Text Edit (0.038) and Formula CDM (95.59). On a 384-page subset and one A800 GPU, it is the fastest end-to-end parser at five concurrency levels, improving valid-page throughput by 67.4-118% and reducing P95 latency by 39.2-54.9% relative to a same-backbone Sequential SFT baseline. Code is available at https://github.com/Longin-Yu/Padoc	2026-08-06 15:16:18+00	2026-08-06 15:16:18+00	https://arxiv.org/pdf/2608.06146v1	{cs.AI}	https://openalex.org/W7201878258	\N	0	2	0.903	EMBEDDED	{"arxiv_id_versioned": "2608.06146v1", "authors_raw": ["Hao Yu", "Jiabo Zhan", "Kang Liu", "Linnan Zhao", "Dongxu Yue", "Rui Chen", "Jinglin Wang", "Chong Sun", "Chen Li", "Jing Lyu", "Chun Yuan"], "primary_category": "cs.AI", "comment": null, "doi": null, "openalex": {"openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/W7201878258", "cited_by_count": 0, "referenced_works_count": 0, "publication_year": 2026, "type": "preprint", "authorships": [{"name": "Hao Yu", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5146002585", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Jiabo Zhan", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5142711093", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Kang Liu", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5146050634", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Linnan Zhao", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5145985890", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Dongxu Yue", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5114231560", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Rui Chen", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5146068526", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Jinglin Wang", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5145958665", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Chong Sun", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5145985736", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Chen Li", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5145942579", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Jing Lyu", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5145993321", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Chun Yuan", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5146004871", "affiliation": null}], "concepts": [{"name": "Computer science", "score": 0.8309000134468079}, {"name": "Decoding methods", "score": 0.6917999982833862}, {"name": "Serialization", "score": 0.6875}, {"name": "Parsing", "score": 0.6765999794006348}, {"name": "Context (archaeology)", "score": 0.4966999888420105}]}, "hn": {"mentions": 2, "total_points": 3, "top_story_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=46928777", "top_story_points": 2}}	2026-08-07 13:50:22.419217+00	2026-08-29 16:24:49.556336+00
78	2608.06144	FinEvo-Bench: A Longitudinal Benchmark for Self-Evolving Agents in Professional Financial Workflows	Most agent benchmarks evaluate tasks independently and cannot measure whether experience from one task helps with later tasks. Existing self-evolution benchmarks do not jointly cover professional workflows, open-ended deliverables, and multi-aspect evaluation. We introduce FinEvo-Bench, a longitudinal benchmark with 120 real-case-grounded tasks, 20 business scenes across six financial domains. Institution-provided professional procedures define the required operations and constraints. Eligible institution-provided and publicly documented cases supply the task facts. Each scene contains six related but substantively distinct cases that share a professional procedure and a manually reviewed rubric for task quality and financial compliance. We compare four self-evolving agent scaffolds using the same Qwen3.7-Max backbone and three independently shuffled, globally interleaved task streams. Paired non-evolving controls estimate each scaffold's self-evolution gain from retained experience, while an independent Claude Code scoring agent backed by Claude Opus 4.6 evaluates all outputs. Letta achieves the highest evolved score (91.65) and fewest compliance issues (0.09 per task); Codex achieves the largest self-evolution gain (+19.37). Across scaffolds, the evolving condition raises scores by 9.33-19.37 points and reduces compliance issues by 0.12-0.44 per task. Paired score gains at within-scene ranks 4-6 exceed those at ranks 1-3 by 6.10-8.70 points. In Claude Code, skill-only evolution produces higher task quality and fewer compliance issues than memory-only and combined memory-skill evolution. Across all four scaffolds, rubric feedback also yields higher scores and fewer compliance issues than reference-answer feedback. FinEvo-Bench measures both professional performance and self-evolution ability: how effectively an agent turns prior experience into later improvement.	2026-08-06 15:14:54+00	2026-08-06 15:14:54+00	https://arxiv.org/pdf/2608.06144v1	{cs.AI}	https://openalex.org/W7201871502	\N	0	1	0.452	EMBEDDED	{"arxiv_id_versioned": "2608.06144v1", "authors_raw": ["Bo Deng", "Kang Zhou", "Lifan Guo", "Chongyang Tao", "Xuanren Chen", "Chenggang Xie", "Renzhao Liang", "Feng Chen", "Chi Zhang"], "primary_category": "cs.AI", "comment": "22 pages, 4 figures; includes appendices", "doi": null, "openalex": {"openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/W7201871502", "cited_by_count": 0, "referenced_works_count": 0, "publication_year": 2026, "type": "preprint", "authorships": [{"name": "Bo Deng", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5078549346", "affiliation": "Cloud Computing Center"}, {"name": "Kang Zhou", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5146046710", "affiliation": "Cloud Computing Center"}, {"name": "Lifan Guo", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5040112548", "affiliation": "Cloud Computing Center"}, {"name": "Chongyang Tao", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5073065834", "affiliation": "Beihang University"}, {"name": "Xuanren Chen", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5146010720", "affiliation": "Beihang University"}, {"name": "Chenggang Xie", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5138062447", "affiliation": "Beihang University"}, {"name": "Renzhao Liang", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5102592023", "affiliation": "Beihang University"}, {"name": "Feng Chen", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5100352695", "affiliation": "Cloud Computing Center"}, {"name": "Chi Zhang", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5100458229", "affiliation": "Cloud Computing Center"}], "concepts": [{"name": "Rubric", "score": 0.8845000267028809}, {"name": "Benchmark (surveying)", "score": 0.708899974822998}, {"name": "Task (project management)", "score": 0.7069000005722046}, {"name": "Workflow", "score": 0.5720000267028809}, {"name": "Computer science", "score": 0.5598000288009644}]}, "hn": {"mentions": 1, "total_points": 1, "top_st