241	2608.27370	Puro-2B: Poor Lab's Qwen2-1.5B Trained on RTX 5090 within $5090	Language model pretraining has become almost synonymous with prohibitive cost, placing it out of reach for much of the academic and open-source communities. Although strong open-source efforts already exist, including open-weight models and open-source training recipes, a cost-efficient, hardware-accessible, and open-source pretraining recipe has long been missing. Even at a small scale, training Llama-3.2-3B costs over \\$1.5M, and reproducing SmolLM3-3B needs over \\$700K. In this report, we present an open pretraining recipe designed to lower this barrier. Using this recipe, we train a collection of Puro-2B models from scratch on up to 1.4 trillion tokens with FP8 precision on consumer-grade RTX 5090 GPUs. The models in the collection differ in token budgets and selected recipe variants. Our best model is trained at a compute cost of less than \\$6.9K and approaches Qwen2.5-1.5B performance under our evaluation protocol. This cost efficiency is enabled by a combination of approaches, including hardware selection, low-precision training, hyperball optimization, curriculum model averaging, and the data recipe. Beyond the recipe itself, we provide two additional results. First, across the Puro-2B collection, we derive a Puro Cost Scaling Law that relates training cost to average model performance; the fitted law suggests that about \\$4.4K, less than \\$5,090, is sufficient to reach the performance of Qwen2-1.5B. Second, as an end-to-end case study, we examine how pretraining data curricula shape downstream performance after post-training. Such controlled studies are enabled by having access to the full pretraining pipeline rather than model weights alone. We release the full training recipe for Puro-2B, including data, code, and model weights under Apache 2.0 at https://huggingface.co/collections/thu-pacman/puro-2b.	2026-08-27 17:07:12+00	2026-08-27 17:07:12+00	https://arxiv.org/pdf/2608.27370v1	{cs.CL,cs.LG}	https://openalex.org/W7204562970	\N	0	2	1.048	EMBEDDED	{"arxiv_id_versioned": "2608.27370v1", "authors_raw": ["Kairong Luo", "Jiarui Cui", "Yaorui Yin", "Shengqi Chen", "Yiming Yang", "Linxiang Gao", "Yanmohan Wang", "Mingzhe Zhang", "Kaiyue Wen", "Kaifeng Lyu", "Wenguang Chen"], "primary_category": "cs.CL", "comment": "62 pages, 20 figures, 24 tables", "doi": null, "openalex": {"openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/W7204562970", "cited_by_count": 0, "referenced_works_count": 0, "publication_year": 2026, "type": "preprint", "authorships": [{"name": "Kairong Luo", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5044575083", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Jiarui Cui", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5039506025", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Yaorui Yin", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5148544512", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Shengqi Chen", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5101491052", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Yiming Yang", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5148494557", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Linxiang Gao", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5076567619", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Yanmohan Wang", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5148523211", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Mingzhe Zhang", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5148509610", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Kaiyue Wen", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5148514824", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Kaifeng Lyu", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5148472260", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Wenguang Chen", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5148484205", "affiliation": null}], "concepts": [{"name": "Recipe", "score": 0.9221000075340271}, {"name": "Pipeline (software)", "score": 0.6575000286102295}, {"name": "Computer science", "score": 0.6054999828338623}, {"name": "Training (meteorology)", "score": 0.4763000011444092}, {"name": "Security token", "score": 0.46970000863075256}]}, "hn": {"mentions": 2, "total_points": 4, "top_story