438	2608.26750	Discovering Relationships in Data Lakes Using Large Language Models: An Industrial Case	Data lakes rely on metadata to remain usable, yet this meta data is often limited or weakly informative for column relationship discovery, especially in ERP-derived datasets with coded or abbreviated schema labels. We propose ColRel, a two-stage method that builds column embeddings from metadata and data available at ingestion time. In difficult cases, such as coded schemata, business dictionaries help better interpret column names and support the generation of short natural-language descriptions used in the second stage. Experiments on public benchmarks and an industrial ERP dataset show that ColRel is particularly effective in semantically related, weak-signal settings.	2026-08-27 07:44:39+00	2026-08-27 07:44:39+00	https://arxiv.org/pdf/2608.26750v1	{cs.AI}	https://openalex.org/W7162354353	\N	0	0	0	EMBEDDED	{"arxiv_id_versioned": "2608.26750v1", "authors_raw": ["Ahlame Diouan", "Eric Ferey", "Sabine Loudcher", "J\\u00e9r\\u00f4me Darmont"], "primary_category": "cs.AI", "comment": null, "doi": null, "openalex": {"openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/W7162354353", "cited_by_count": 0, "referenced_works_count": 0, "publication_year": 2026, "type": "conference-paper", "authorships": [{"name": "Ahlame Diouan", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5038517981", "affiliation": "Seattle Epidemiologic Information and Research Center"}, {"name": "\\u00c9ric Ferey", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5088822615", "affiliation": "Seattle Epidemiologic Information and Research Center"}, {"name": "Sabine Loudcher", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5004311434", "affiliation": "Seattle Epidemiologic Information and Research Center"}, {"name": "J\\u00e9r\\u00f4me Darmont", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5080624394", "affiliation": "Seattle Epidemiologic Information and Research Center"}], "concepts": [{"name": "Computer science", "score": 0.43689998984336853}, {"name": "Remote sensing", "score": 0.35989999771118164}, {"name": "Geography", "score": 0.3089999854564667}, {"name": "Field (mathematics)", "score": 0.30219998955726624}, {"name": "Identification (biology)", "score": 0.3012000024318695}]}, "hn": {"mentions": 0, "total_points": 0, "top_story_url": null, "top_story_points": 0}}	2026-08-29 16:08:23.427975+00	2026-08-29 18:57:14.016985+00
439	2608.26749	Letters hide the truth from our eyes: English homophones have meaningfully different phonetic realizations	The distribution of spoken word duration of English homophones is known to co-vary with frequency of use. This study investigates whether other aspects of the phonetic realization of homophones also differ. A series of quantitative investigations of 14,000 homophone tokens in American television news broadcasts revealed that the tokens of homophone pairs such as \\textit{weight} and \\textit{wait} have different phonetic realizations, and that these can be predicted from their meanings in utterance context. These systematic differences remain even when taking duration-related variation into account. Time-normalized spectrograms emerged as an excellent tool for probing the fine details of phonetic realization, and obviate the need for phonetic transcriptions, which inevitably hide the phonetic truth from our eyes.	2026-08-27 07:44:14+00	2026-08-27 07:44:14+00	https://arxiv.org/pdf/2608.26749v1	{cs.CL}	https://openalex.org/W7204565519	\N	0	0	0	EMBEDDED	{"arxiv_id_versioned": "2608.26749v1", "authors_raw": ["Yu-Hsiang Tseng", "Mirjam T. C. Ernestus", "Louis F. M. ten Bosch", "R. Harald Baayen"], "primary_category": "cs.CL", "comment": "54 pages, 9 figures", "doi": null, "openalex": {"openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/W7204565519", "cited_by_count": 0, "referenced_works_count": 0, "publication_year": 2026, "type": "preprint", "authorships": [{"name": "Yu-Hsiang Tseng", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5018548772", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Mirjam Ernestus", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5091677603", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "Louis F. M. ten Bosch", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5078246969", "affiliation": null}, {"name": "R. Harald Baayen", "openalex_id": "https://openalex.org/A5148512768", "affiliation": null}], "concepts": [{"name": "Homophone", "score": 0.9937000274658203}, {"name": "Utterance", "score": 0.679300